From 4a400961056f4e746e1176332e59cf8f6b6b762a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:11:37 +0100
Subject: WindowManagerService: allow rotating without the screen rotation
 animation

The rotation animation turns the screen through angles that are not one of the
eight HWC2 transforms, so SurfaceFlinger must render those frames itself on
every display it draws. While a mini-HDMI mirror is up that costs the mirror:
the composer declines it for as long as any layer on the external display is
client composited.

Skipping the animation while a second display is attached removes those frames
entirely -- rotation becomes a jump cut, and the panel keeps its animation
whenever nothing is mirrored. Measured with this on: no layer anywhere carries
ROT_INVALID, and the external display receives no client composition marks.

It is not on by default: on its own it does not keep the mirror alive, because
the external is lost for reasons that outlive rotation. It is committed as an
option because it is the only known way to stop rotation producing intermediate
transforms without zeroing the user's animation scales.

Changes:
- `WindowManagerService.java`: skip creating `ScreenRotationAnimation` in `startFreezingDisplay()` when more than one display is attached, gated on `persist.sys.xdplus.mirror_no_rot_anim` (default off)

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: If103d4784bd5d7cd5525fdbe397c76a2868f355b
---
 .../java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
index 03b22e52..0677217e 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
@@ -5628,6 +5628,15 @@ public class WindowManagerService extends IWindowManager.Stub
         final int originalRotation = overrideOriginalRotation != ROTATION_UNDEFINED
                 ? overrideOriginalRotation
                 : displayContent.getDisplayInfo().rotation;
+
+        // Its intermediate angles are no HWC2 transform, forcing client composition and losing
+        // the external mirror.
+        if (mRoot.getChildCount() > 1
+                && SystemProperties.getBoolean("persist.sys.xdplus.mirror_no_rot_anim", false)) {
+            displayContent.setRotationAnimation(null);
+            return;
+        }
+
         displayContent.setRotationAnimation(new ScreenRotationAnimation(displayContent,
                 originalRotation));
     }
